-- title:
--   Slope-drop function at a supersingular node on subdivided depths
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N\ge 1$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring map $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$, a place specialisation $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q\nmid N$, that $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws), that $R$ satisfies the fixed-place order law, and fix a finite set $W_0$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$, all supersingular, for which $R$ satisfies the regularity law and the node value law. Fix intermediate fields $K\le K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ with $K'$ finite over $\mathbb Q$, a place $w\in W_0$ whose arithmetic Frobenius translate $\varphi w=\mathrm{arithFrobC}\,q\,k\,N\cdot w$ also lies in $W_0$, the value integrality law at $w$, and the inclusion $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K\,w\le R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$. Fix $\varpi\in A\cap K'$ whose multiples are exactly the elements killed by $\mathrm{red}$, $e_K\ge 1$ and a unit $\varepsilon$ with $q=\varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$. Fix node coordinates $c=(x,y)$ over $K$ at $w$ (so $x$ has first residue $0$ and second residue of order $1$ at $\varphi w$, while $y$ has second residue $0$ and first residue of order $1$ at $w$), integers $e_w,e'\ge 1$, and a unit $u$ of $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ with the node equation $xy=(\mathrm{nodeConst}\,K'\,w\,\varpi)^{e_we_K}u$. Assume further that the ideal generated by $\varpi,x,y$ in $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ is maximal and is the only maximal ideal, that this ring is local and Noetherian with that ideal as maximal ideal, that $(\varpi,x)$ and $(\varpi,y)$ are prime with $y\notin(\varpi,x)$ and $x\notin(\varpi,y)$, and that every element of the ring becomes a non-unit after subtracting a suitable constant. Let $\mathrm{depth}$ assign a natural number to each place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $f\ne 0$ lie in that field with its Laurent expansion in $\mathrm{fieldOver}\,(Nq)\,K'$, and assume every element of $\mathrm{fieldOver}\,(Nq)\,K'$ is a ratio of two elements of $R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\,K'\,w$ with non-zero denominator. Let $c_1,c_2\in K'$ be non-zero with $c_1f$ in the integers of $R.R_1$ and $c_2f$ in those of $R.R_2$, both with non-zero residue. Let $D$ be the divisor $V\mapsto V.\mathrm{ord}\,f$, assume $(c.\mathrm{yDepth}\,V)^{e'}=|q|_A^{\mathrm{depth}\,V}$ for every $V$ in the support of $D$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w$, and assume the node total $\sum_{V:\ P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w}D(V)=\mathrm{ord}_w(R.\mathrm{residue}_1(c_1f))+\mathrm{ord}_{\varphi w}(R.\mathrm{residue}_2(c_2f))$. Then there is $G:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ such that for every $d$ with $1\le d<e'e_w$ the slope drop $(G(d)-G(d-1))-(G(d+1)-G(d))$ equals the sum of $D(V)$ over the places $V$ in the support of $D$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w$ and $\mathrm{depth}\,V=d$; moreover $G(1)-G(0)=\mathrm{ord}_w(R.\mathrm{residue}_1(c_1f))$, $G(e'e_w)-G(e'e_w-1)=-\mathrm{ord}_{\varphi w}(R.\mathrm{residue}_2(c_2f))$, and $|c_1/c_2|_A^{e'}=|q|_A^{G(e'e_w)-G(0)}$ in the value group of $A$.
--
--   This is the concavity (slope-drop) bookkeeping for a principal divisor at a supersingular node of the Deligne–Rapoport style model: the multiplicities of the divisor at the places over the node, graded by the $e'$-fold subdivided depth of the node parameter $y$, are realised as second differences of a single integer function on $\{0,\dots,e'e_w\}$, whose end slopes are the orders of the two residues and whose total increment records the valuation of the scaling ratio $c_1/c_2$. It is the version with general subdivision factor $e'$, so that the end-to-end exponent need only match $|c_1/c_2|^{e'}$, and it feeds the statements `depthDual_add_mem_range_gramMap_of_isPrincipal` and `depthDual_add_mem_range_gramMap_of_isPrincipal_widthChar`.
